# Spring Boot Java 25 Standards

Apply these rules in all tasks for this repository.

## Language and naming
- Write class names, method names, attribute names, variables, constants, packages, and comments in English.
- Use meaningful domain names (`ReservationService`, `CreateReservationRequest`), avoid abbreviations.
- Follow Java naming conventions: `PascalCase` for classes, `camelCase` for methods/fields, `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE` for constants.

## API and DTO conventions
- Every public method must include up-to-date Javadoc with purpose, params, return value, and thrown exceptions.
- Use Java `record` for DTOs (request/response and immutable transport models).
- Keep controllers thin: validate input and delegate business logic to services.

## Spring Boot architecture
- Use layered architecture: Controller -> Service -> Repository.
- Inject dependencies by constructor only (prefer `final` fields, no field injection).
- Keep transactional boundaries in service layer with `@Transactional` when needed.
- Use `@RestControllerAdvice` for centralized exception handling and consistent error responses.

## Java 25 and code quality
- Prefer immutability and small, focused classes/methods.
- Use modern Java features when they improve readability and safety.
- Validate inputs early and fail fast with explicit exceptions.
- Add/maintain unit and integration tests for business logic and endpoints.

## Package layout (source tree)

Use one base Java package for the application and **mirror the package name in the folder path** (e.g. `.../reservation_backend/service/MyService.java` for `...reservation_backend.service`).

**Base package:** `com.florhiembuchner.web.reservation_backend` (only the main application class may sit directly under this package).

| Subpackage (under base) | Folder path segment | Place here |
|-------------------------|---------------------|------------|
| `.config` | `config/` | `@Configuration` classes, `CorsFilter` and other web/security beans, property beans |
| `.controller` | `controller/` | `@RestController` classes; HTTP mapping only |
| `.service` | `service/` | `@Service` classes; business rules and `@Transactional` orchestration |
| `.repository` | `repository/` | Spring Data interfaces (`JpaRepository`, etc.) |
| `.entity` | `entity/` | JPA `@Entity` classes and enums used as persisted types |
| `.dto` | `dto/` | Request/response `record`s and API payload models |
| `.mapper` | `mapper/` | Mappers between entities and DTOs (manual or MapStruct) |
| `.exception` | `exception/` | Domain exceptions, `@RestControllerAdvice`, shared error response types |

Do not mix layers in one package (e.g. do not put entities under `service/`).

## Non-Java resources and tests

- `reservation-backend/src/main/resources` — `application.properties`, SQL scripts, Flyway/Liquibase migrations if used.
- `reservation-backend/src/test/java` — mirror the main package tree for unit and integration tests (`...Test` / `...IT` next to or under parallel packages as the project convention dictates).
